# NestJS Module Structure

Every NestJS module must follow the required structure:

- interfaces/
- repository/
- service/
- controller/
- controller/dto/
- test/
- {module}.module.ts

Repositories:

- Implement `I{Module}Repository`.
- Contain Prisma/data access only.
- Must not throw HTTP exceptions.
- Return `null` or result objects when data is missing.

Services:

- Implement `I{Module}Service`.
- Own business rules and exceptions.
- Throw `NotFoundException`, `BadRequestException`, `ConflictException`, etc. when appropriate.
- Must enforce tenant safety.

Controllers:

- Inject services only.
- Do not inject repositories.
- Do not contain business logic.
- Do not accept `tenantId` from request body.

Tests:

- Controller tests mock the service.
- Service tests mock the repository.
- Keep tests under `test/`.

After module changes, run:

- `node scripts/validate-structure.js`
